From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 09:55:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] procd: cancel the boot scripts still running when the
 shutdown starts

procd's rcS kept one runqueue for the boot's and the shutdown's init
scripts, one script at a time, and set it up anew for the shutdown
without the count of running scripts: a boot script that never
returned kept the only slot, the shutdown ran none of its K scripts,
and a reboot never completed. On the emulator, a uci-defaults script
looping forever during a trial boot left the system in "- shutdown -"
for ten minutes, until the test gave up; wrt-ab's trial deadline
reboots exactly then (trial-guards D6).

Carry the procd patch that cancels the boot's scripts when the
shutdown starts: those yet to start are dropped, the running one gets
SIGTERM and, 10 s later, SIGKILL, as a shutdown script past its time
does. It is meant for procd upstream.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 package/system/procd/Makefile                 |  2 +-
 ...ill-running-when-the-shutdown-starts.patch | 77 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 78 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 package/system/procd/patches/103-rcS-cancel-the-boot-scripts-still-running-when-the-shutdown-starts.patch

diff --git a/package/system/procd/Makefile b/package/system/procd/Makefile
index 9a66dd5..4bc324f 100644
--- a/package/system/procd/Makefile
+++ b/package/system/procd/Makefile
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@
 include $(TOPDIR)/rules.mk
 
 PKG_NAME:=procd
-PKG_RELEASE:=6
+PKG_RELEASE:=7
 
 PKG_SOURCE_PROTO:=git
 PKG_SOURCE_URL=$(PROJECT_GIT)/project/procd.git
diff --git a/package/system/procd/patches/103-rcS-cancel-the-boot-scripts-still-running-when-the-shutdown-starts.patch b/package/system/procd/patches/103-rcS-cancel-the-boot-scripts-still-running-when-the-shutdown-starts.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..08fb691
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/system/procd/patches/103-rcS-cancel-the-boot-scripts-still-running-when-the-shutdown-starts.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,77 @@
+From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] rcS: cancel the boot scripts still running when the shutdown starts
+
+rcS() set its one runqueue up anew for every run: runqueue_init()
+emptied the task lists but left the count of running tasks, which
+the next run's limit of one task counts against. A shutdown that
+started while a boot script still ran, one waiting for a device that
+never comes or hung in a loop, therefore never ran a K script: the
+boot script kept the only slot until it returned, which it may never
+do, and the system never reached its halt. A reboot from an init
+script or from userspace then hung with it.
+
+Cancel the previous run instead: the boot's scripts yet to start are
+dropped, and the one running gets SIGTERM and, 10 s later, SIGKILL,
+as a shutdown script that overruns its time does. The shutdown's
+scripts start once it has ended. The queue is set up once, as the
+queue of single init scripts is, and a script dropped before it
+started closes no output, since it has none.
+
+Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+---
+ rcS.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++----
+ 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
+
+diff --git a/rcS.c b/rcS.c
+index 1e36c98..34ab105 100644
+--- a/rcS.c
++++ b/rcS.c
+@@ -114,6 +114,12 @@ static void q_initd_complete(struct runqueue *q, struct runqueue_task *p)
+ 	struct initd *s = container_of(p, struct initd, proc.task);
+ 	struct timespec ts_stop, ts_res;
+ 
++	/* Dropped before it started: no output to close. */
++	if (s->fd.fd.fd < 0) {
++		free(s);
++		return;
++	}
++
+ 	clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW, &ts_stop);
+ 	ts_res.tv_sec = ts_stop.tv_sec - s->ts_start.tv_sec;
+ 	ts_res.tv_nsec = ts_stop.tv_nsec - s->ts_start.tv_nsec;
+@@ -160,10 +166,10 @@ static void add_initd(struct runqueue *q, const char *file, const char *param)
+ 	}
+ 	s->proc.task.type = &initd_type;
+ 	s->proc.task.complete = q_initd_complete;
+-	if (!strcmp(param, "stop") || !strcmp(param, "shutdown")) {
++	s->proc.task.cancel_timeout = 10000;
++	if (!strcmp(param, "stop") || !strcmp(param, "shutdown"))
+ 		s->proc.task.run_timeout = 15000;
+-		s->proc.task.cancel_timeout = 10000;
+-	}
++	s->fd.fd.fd = -1;
+ 	s->param = p;
+ 	s->file = f;
+ 	strcpy(s->param, param);
+@@ -199,7 +205,12 @@ static int _rc(struct runqueue *q, const char *path, const char *file, const cha
+ 
+ int rcS(const char *pattern, const char *param, void (*q_empty)(struct runqueue *))
+ {
+-	runqueue_init(&q);
++	/*
++	 * A shutdown may start while a boot script still runs, one that may
++	 * never return: drop the boot's scripts yet to start and cancel the
++	 * running one, which the shutdown's scripts then wait for alone.
++	 */
++	runqueue_cancel(&q);
+ 	q.empty_cb = q_empty;
+ 	q.max_running_tasks = 1;
+ 
+@@ -217,6 +228,7 @@ static void r_empty(struct runqueue *q)
+ }
+ 
+ static void __attribute__((constructor)) rc_init() {
++	runqueue_init(&q);
+ 	runqueue_init(&r);
+ 	r.empty_cb = r_empty;
+ 	r.max_running_tasks = 8;
